WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.396
Turn podcast audio into structured text with en eight en and Apify.

2
00:00:04.396 --> 00:00:07.693
This is a supervised starter for self hosted setups.

3
00:00:07.693 --> 00:00:13.188
We will use configuration diagrams and saved test evidence, rather than a
live screen recording.

4
00:00:13.188 --> 00:00:16.851
The template is free; Apify Actor usage is billed separately.

5
00:00:18.051 --> 00:00:25.804
The workflow reads episode entries from an R S S feed, validates their
audio enclosure links, and removes duplicates within the batch.

6
00:00:25.804 --> 00:00:28.624
It sends those links to the Apify integration.

7
00:00:28.624 --> 00:00:30.386
All returned rows stay visible.

8
00:00:30.386 --> 00:00:34.615
Replace the final output stub with your own storage and error handling.

9
00:00:34.615 --> 00:00:37.787
The feed cursor is not a durable delivery ledger.

10
00:00:38.987 --> 00:00:44.329
Install the official Apify community node, then download the workflow JSON
from the linked guide.

11
00:00:44.329 --> 00:00:51.808
On en eight en version two point forty point five, the directory import
command shown here generates a local workflow identifier.

12
00:00:51.808 --> 00:00:56.082
A direct single file import without an identifier failed in our check.

13
00:00:56.082 --> 00:00:59.287
Keep the imported workflow inactive while you configure it.

14
00:01:00.487 --> 00:01:03.172
Attach your own Apify credential to Transcribe episode.

15
00:01:03.172 --> 00:01:05.857
Never paste the token into the workflow JSON.

16
00:01:05.857 --> 00:01:08.877
Keep the prefilled Actor identifier in I D mode.

17
00:01:08.877 --> 00:01:15.925
The username and Actor name alias works in the web A P I, but this en eight
en field rejects it.

18
00:01:15.925 --> 00:01:22.637
For the short test, change the template's one dollar limit to five cents,
with five hundred twelve megabytes of memory.

19
00:01:23.837 --> 00:01:26.522
For a manual check, make a temporary copy.

20
00:01:26.522 --> 00:01:31.557
Replace the R S S trigger with a manual trigger followed by a Code node.

21
00:01:31.557 --> 00:01:36.256
Connect it to Extract audio U R L, and paste this short test entry.

22
00:01:36.256 --> 00:01:38.942
The public sample is about twenty six seconds.

23
00:01:38.942 --> 00:01:44.648
At the verified managed price, it rounds to one minute: one cent plus the
small start event.

24
00:01:45.848 --> 00:01:50.476
Our saved live check included a duplicate sample and an unsupported video
page.

25
00:01:50.476 --> 00:01:54.036
The workflow submitted two unique links in one Actor run.

26
00:01:54.036 --> 00:01:59.375
It returned one real transcript with S R T subtitles, and one visible error
row.

27
00:01:59.375 --> 00:02:02.935
Platform counts confirmed one transcription minute and one start event.

28
00:02:02.935 --> 00:02:07.563
A succeeded status alone does not mean that every input produced a
transcript.

29
00:02:08.763 --> 00:02:13.709
Return to the original workflow and set your feed U R L and poll interval.

30
00:02:13.709 --> 00:02:20.634
Choose a budget that covers the intended episode length; the five cent demo
limit is not suitable for a long podcast.

31
00:02:20.634 --> 00:02:23.272
Configure persistent results and a workflow error destination.

32
00:02:23.272 --> 00:02:28.878
We have verified the manual Apify path, but have not certified live feed
polling or restart recovery.

33
00:02:30.079 --> 00:02:35.880
A per run budget is not a total limit for all retries or for the month.

34
00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:41.682
The integration can retry rate limit and server errors internally, even
with node level retries off.

35
00:02:41.682 --> 00:02:44.220
Manual replays can also create another charge.

36
00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:47.120
Inspect the existing Apify run and dataset first.

37
00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:51.834
A production pipeline needs persistent episode tracking and explicit
recovery for uncertain work.

38
00:02:53.033 --> 00:02:57.815
The workflow and current setup guide are available in the repository shown
here.

39
00:02:57.815 --> 00:03:05.907
Start with one useful transcript, inspect every output type, and validate
your own feed and recovery behavior before relying on unattended operation.

40
00:03:05.907 --> 00:03:08.850
Use the Actor's pricing page for current rates.
